<title>HONG KONG: COSCO Pacific interim net rises 47.4 pct.</title>
<headline>COSCO Pacific interim net rises 47.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million US$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (U.S. cents)	   1.95  vs 2.15 (see note)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    6.00  vs 6.28</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil   vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    32.40 vs 21.98</p>
<p>    Turnover		     68.91 vs 58.57</p>
<p>    Company name		 COSCO Pacific Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  October 22-25</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   October 28</p>
<p>NOTE - China-owned container leasing firm COSCO Pacific is controlled by its largest customer China Ocean Shipping (Group) Co (COSCO).</p>
<p>Share earnings are based on a weighted average of 1.66 billion vs 1.02 billion.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
